+- **SSH receive-window policy**: Core now selects bounded 32 KiB, 64 KiB,
+  capped-BDP, and relay-burst initial credit, then reconciles per-channel,
+  per-lane, global-window, and global-ledger reservations across adjustments
+  and lifecycle release. The selected libssh2 adapter consumes the bounded
+  initial value while continuing to report consumer-driven adjustment as
+  unsupported until its M3 engine work lands.
+- **Memory watermark controller**: Core samples current process footprint and
+  one uncached advisory value behind a platform seam, combines them with fresh
+  shared-ledger evidence, and serializes Soft, Pressure, Critical, and
+  one-step hysteretic recovery transitions. Cadence, event bursts, sample age,
+  execution classification, retained history, and metric cardinality are all
+  configured and bounded; unavailable evidence is never replaced with zero.
 
